<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcad094f4a9f7f57f486e175adf4a7fddc27e16b2628019f32c6322923422652</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191--0ec0144d606e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Picasso to Andy Warhol, a surprising number of artists have portrayed the German breed. But the dachshund has also at times been co-opted as a political symbol.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz hopes for Korean reunification at DMZ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3402b8d319ab24d008bbc6410c86be6a1a008e684fbbc7965621ae34cb5d675</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462--f2cebaec800e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has expressed hope for Korean reunification during a visit to the heavily fortified border. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier has held talks with China's Xi Jinping in Beijing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayer wins Roundup cancer trial after Supreme Court ruling</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0231697f73e1c8d96334b7cbbca95dfce75a3bdd7212cafe38e1052d2d983af5</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T02:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayer-wins-roundup-cancer-trial-after-supreme-court-ruling/a-79803301--b3d21555ad34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayer-wins-roundup-cancer-trial-after-supreme-court-ruling/a-79803301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The weedkiller Roundup has been accused of being carcinogenic to humans despite no warning on its label. Bayer is seeking to settle tens of thousands of further cases.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Alexander Zverev clinches tennis No. 1 ranking</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff2dc02316bdab1e5582c709020d821ad29d9112632bfc396d6db6ce88e6fa81</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048--1b03a09b61b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev is the second German man, after Boris Becker, to clinch the No. 1 spot in tennis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin's Elif Eralp under fire over Der Spiegel interview</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f420572f94dcacf1adf9340186040ee842fada21f27ad6c444aaea8ae101a96a</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T20:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-elif-eralp-under-fire-over-der-spiegel-interview/a-79799766--cde8b7af3fbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-elif-eralp-under-fire-over-der-spiegel-interview/a-79799766?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Left candidate Elif Eralp has sparked controversy after Der Spiegel reported she was advised against mentioning a pro-Palestinian activist for fear of reprisals against her family.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Chancellor Friedrich Merz accuses North Korea of threatening Europe's freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:967de74fe89f4c566a45648f43b70bf0f73bdcec85c7c68310d912edb3982970</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915--91e1e32cf271.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Friedrich Merz, who is visiting Seoul, said North Korea is putting Europe's security at risk by sending soldiers to fight for Russia in Ukraine. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbb79ea56d16f6da20cae9ce9eaad49f4b9bb5a006689859361aa864b8b4aa1a</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184--6eb977f23eb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German politicians have been slow to respond as they wait to see who is likely to comprise the next coalition. Many are also hoping for a government without religious hardliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks new head of state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58cd3ef5736ce8549653d2db45ccd8bd390764681cb68e6987d48e5c8301410c</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794--10071c049ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The question of who should become Germany's new presiden is becoming pressing. Many want to see Germany's first female head of state. Chancellor Friedrich Merz is keeping his cards close to his chest.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen logs Q3 operating loss of €5.86 billion on Porsche writedown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e14e79ded2949f101d4e45f53c3d8ae12662072fc9ef6d3382feb584725f713</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-_5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796--74f8be5771cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-€5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Volkswagen Group has filed its worst quarterly performance since the height of the "Dieselgate" scandal in 2015. Share prices climbed in response, however, perhaps because the bad news was so well signposted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany's health scare highlights the need for better support for elite coaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b610c1c5f59b26d3fb7f720448710d82d901837e3349fa66e9c10a03ea29c84</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-e/a-79764661--fcbaed2aac2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-elite-coaches/a-79764661?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vincent Kompany’s health concern is a reminder that elite football's pressures affect coaches too. Better support, clearer structures and mental health safeguards are increasingly vital.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1c4a17104858ee9be801111eec1c5da027abd9daf4fc2dfb72f9d6edb16e75a</id><updated>2026-10-31T05:57:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
